WEBVTT

01:00.390 --> 01:07.230
It is said that 70% of the
human brain's capacity is unused.

01:09.230 --> 01:11.290
It's also thought that...

01:11.870 --> 01:15.060
...the mysterious powers that humans
have are hidden in this part of the brain.

01:17.010 --> 01:21.570
The 70% of the brain that is not used...

01:22.340 --> 01:24.070
...is often called this...

01:24.150 --> 01:29.880
<i>Night Head Genesis</i>

01:30.850 --> 01:31.920
<i>Memories</i>

01:31.920 --> 01:35.880
<i>Episode 1
Memories</i>

01:54.140 --> 01:55.910
What's the matter, Naoya?

01:56.010 --> 01:58.540
You're such a good boy.
Don't cry, Naoya-chan.

02:15.000 --> 02:15.960
Naoto!

02:20.440 --> 02:22.200
A student got hurt!

02:22.270 --> 02:24.900
When Naoto-kun got mad,
Matsumo-kun got a nosebleed.

02:26.170 --> 02:27.160
That's scary...

02:27.810 --> 02:29.540
Naoto-kun, you're scary.

02:31.410 --> 02:36.040
Naoto, you don't have to go to
school anymore for a little while.

02:42.720 --> 02:45.390
Hey, what are you doing, damn it!

02:45.830 --> 02:47.490
Why isn't it moving!

02:47.760 --> 02:51.260
Brother, everyone is saying lies.

02:54.440 --> 02:57.200
Has Naoya-kun become
like this any other time?

02:57.270 --> 03:00.400
When he touches someone and
sees something he doesn't like.

03:00.480 --> 03:02.670
What do you mean by sees?

03:02.880 --> 03:07.080
When Naoya touches someone, he
can read the inside of his or her heart.

03:07.420 --> 03:10.540
So he sees lots of things he
doesn't like that make Naoya...

03:10.790 --> 03:14.310
It's impossible to not let him touch
anyone for the rest of his life.

03:49.260 --> 03:51.820
Naoya, why don't you come over
here and have some cake?

04:01.800 --> 04:03.900
Naoya, what's the matter?

04:04.770 --> 04:05.740
Yeah.

04:23.160 --> 04:24.890
I knew.

04:25.390 --> 04:29.390
That there were drugs
in the melon soda...

04:53.290 --> 04:54.380
Honey!

04:56.630 --> 05:02.960
This is the best thing to do for
the life of Naoto-kun and Naoya-kun.

05:08.500 --> 05:09.300
Wait!

05:09.300 --> 05:09.790
Wait!
Naomi!

05:11.970 --> 05:13.070
I'm sorry!

05:16.780 --> 05:19.040
Please forgive your mother! I'm sorry!

05:21.880 --> 05:22.940
Mom...

05:25.120 --> 05:26.920
No, where are they taking us?

05:27.260 --> 05:28.240
Naomi!

05:28.590 --> 05:29.990
Let's not do this.

05:31.460 --> 05:33.150
I can't bear to be separated from them.

05:33.230 --> 05:34.890
Right, honey?

05:35.230 --> 05:37.930
I'm sad too, but we have no choice!

05:38.300 --> 05:39.930
Let me out of here!

05:51.250 --> 05:51.970
Naoto!

06:03.220 --> 06:08.180
It was painful and sad,
so I ran into my dreams.

06:16.500 --> 06:21.940
In my dream, the sound of Mom crying
was echoing the whole time.

07:26.640 --> 07:28.270
Where am I?

07:28.440 --> 07:29.840
Where is this place!

07:31.080 --> 07:33.340
Damn it! They put stuff like this on me!

07:46.460 --> 07:50.900
Are you the ones that brought
Naoya and me to a place like this?

08:16.520 --> 08:17.550
Naoya!

08:18.390 --> 08:19.220
Brother...

08:23.330 --> 08:24.260
Naoya...

08:26.530 --> 08:27.870
We were abandoned...

08:28.600 --> 08:30.700
We were abandoned by our parents!

08:31.240 --> 08:33.300
It's only Naoya and me now.

08:33.540 --> 08:35.370
We were abandoned!

08:37.250 --> 08:38.010
Brother...

08:38.450 --> 08:39.670
Damn it!

08:40.080 --> 08:42.110
I'm not going to hold it in anymore!

08:47.320 --> 08:48.760
Stop it, Naoto!

08:51.060 --> 08:51.960
Naoto...

08:52.930 --> 08:54.420
It's dangerous, Mikuriya-sensei!

08:55.360 --> 08:56.800
Listen carefully, Naoto.

08:57.070 --> 08:59.470
You guys cannot go back
to your home anymore.

08:59.700 --> 09:02.690
From now on, I am taking
the place of your parents.

09:02.840 --> 09:04.530
This is your home.

09:04.810 --> 09:07.270
You will live here with us.

09:07.410 --> 09:08.500
No!

09:19.090 --> 09:22.160
Naoto, you will stay here with Naoya...

09:22.160 --> 09:23.560
Naoto, you will stay here with Naoya...
We're going home.

09:25.390 --> 09:26.450
Let's go, Naoya.

09:26.790 --> 09:27.620
Yeah.

09:31.430 --> 09:32.460
Naoto!

09:33.570 --> 09:34.900
Naoya!

09:42.180 --> 09:42.940
I'm going home.

09:45.880 --> 09:47.310
I'm going back to our house!

09:48.150 --> 09:49.510
Together with Naoya...

09:50.320 --> 09:51.410
I'm going home!

10:16.410 --> 10:17.470
Brother...

10:17.780 --> 10:19.470
What are those?

10:20.680 --> 10:21.480
It doesn't matter!

10:56.650 --> 10:57.680
What?

11:07.100 --> 11:08.190
Damn it!

11:13.530 --> 11:14.800
What is this!

11:23.950 --> 11:25.140
Damn it!

11:25.350 --> 11:26.900
What is there!

11:31.150 --> 11:33.280
What's going on! Damn it!

11:33.820 --> 11:36.480
Why can't we get through? Why!

11:36.990 --> 11:38.190
Damn it!

11:57.650 --> 11:58.580
Brother...

11:58.710 --> 12:00.080
I'm sorry, Naoya.

12:00.450 --> 12:02.040
I shouldn't be crying.

12:03.690 --> 12:05.020
I'm sorry, Naoya.

12:21.070 --> 12:22.230
Naoto-san.

12:25.210 --> 12:27.270
Please, d-don't do anything.

12:27.540 --> 12:28.600
Take this.

12:28.780 --> 12:30.870
There's warm tea in it.

12:31.180 --> 12:32.110
Please.

12:32.180 --> 12:33.880
There are drugs in it too, right?

12:33.950 --> 12:36.350
There isn't! It's only tea.

12:44.560 --> 12:46.650
It's cold. Let's go back.

12:46.790 --> 12:48.590
If we don't warm you up...

12:48.800 --> 12:50.760
P-Please come back.

13:00.880 --> 13:03.240
Please, please don't do anything!

13:05.050 --> 13:06.070
Naoya...

13:11.590 --> 13:13.140
We knew.

13:13.920 --> 13:15.550
Both my brother and I knew...

13:18.130 --> 13:21.220
That we could never
go back to that home...

13:24.400 --> 13:27.390
That we had to live here...

13:27.800 --> 13:29.360
Somewhere in our hearts...

14:07.480 --> 14:11.210
<i>15 years later, Tokyo</i>

14:17.750 --> 14:18.840
Shouko?

14:30.100 --> 14:32.760
There was a big accident
on the highway.

14:33.370 --> 14:39.330
If I hadn't done what you told me to do,
I would have been in that accident.

14:43.740 --> 14:44.800
Shouko?

14:58.760 --> 15:01.250
What's wrong, Shouko?
What are those words?

15:03.360 --> 15:07.960
I said I didn't want to go,
and then the trip was cancelled.

15:08.040 --> 15:10.030
My mom was surprised too.

15:10.710 --> 15:13.110
I was saved because of you.

15:13.310 --> 15:14.400
Miki...

15:16.280 --> 15:19.010
Miki, you won't die at a place like that.

15:19.150 --> 15:22.310
You're going to live a lot longer.

15:22.750 --> 15:26.650
You'll get happily married
and have lots of kids.

15:28.460 --> 15:29.290
What?

15:29.360 --> 15:31.120
I want you to hold on to this.

15:31.330 --> 15:32.420
Why?

15:34.200 --> 15:35.180
Elder Misaki...

15:35.630 --> 15:36.430
What?

15:37.670 --> 15:41.500
Elder Misaki went off
on a trip from this world.

15:43.300 --> 15:45.930
Elder Misaki?

15:48.180 --> 15:50.910
So the barrier disappeared.

15:51.310 --> 15:54.510
Tonight, two brothers will escape.

16:04.290 --> 16:08.060
Miki, please hold on to that
notebook with great care.

16:12.900 --> 16:14.230
What's wrong?

16:14.600 --> 16:15.930
Shouko?

17:16.630 --> 17:17.790
What's wrong, Naoya?

17:19.830 --> 17:20.930
He's looking.

17:21.640 --> 17:24.870
Elder Misaki is staring right at us.

17:32.010 --> 17:32.880
Let's go!

18:32.640 --> 18:34.230
Yes, I've passed it!

18:35.240 --> 18:36.440
I passed it!

18:38.750 --> 18:41.240
Naoya, come on, jump! Jump!

18:42.350 --> 18:43.410
Brother...

18:43.620 --> 18:44.850
Naoya, we're free.

18:45.320 --> 18:47.290
There is a bigger world over here.

18:47.860 --> 18:50.290
We can go anywhere now.

18:50.490 --> 18:51.920
Nothing is scary.

18:52.160 --> 18:52.960
Come on!

18:54.900 --> 18:55.860
Yeah.

19:27.130 --> 19:28.100
Naoya...

19:28.430 --> 19:30.560
I'm always with you.

19:31.770 --> 19:32.600
Yeah.

19:36.100 --> 19:39.130
I was scared of having freedom.

19:39.870 --> 19:44.810
The world of freedom that is spread
infinitely on this side of the rope...

19:55.060 --> 19:56.110
It's the outside.

20:07.130 --> 20:09.760
Mikuriya-san was saying that...

20:10.740 --> 20:15.640
...if we get outside,
we'll call over the negative power.

20:16.580 --> 20:19.010
Don't worry about what that guy said.

20:19.610 --> 20:21.880
He was the one that locked us in.

20:23.680 --> 20:24.670
It's fine.

20:25.190 --> 20:26.980
You and I aren't kids anymore.

20:27.150 --> 20:28.990
We can live wherever we go.

20:29.490 --> 20:30.750
Just like the normal people...

21:01.590 --> 21:02.560
What happened?

21:05.590 --> 21:06.560
Damn it!

21:09.000 --> 21:10.760
Brother, over there...

21:22.340 --> 21:24.370
No, I'll do something about this.

21:24.580 --> 21:25.570
Wait.

21:25.810 --> 21:26.640
What?

21:28.450 --> 21:30.080
You know what I'm going to say.

21:30.580 --> 21:31.880
Say it clearly.

21:33.150 --> 21:35.050
I want to go there.

21:35.990 --> 21:37.320
I want to eat something.

21:37.390 --> 21:40.380
And, Brother, you should rest a little too.

21:40.460 --> 21:43.900
If we go there and ask,
maybe they can take care of it.

21:45.570 --> 21:48.900
Even though you were
shaking in fear before.

22:20.200 --> 22:22.170
We call over...

22:22.540 --> 22:24.160
...the negative power.

22:29.910 --> 22:38.720
<i>I hope that everything that
makes you sad will all disappear.</i>

22:38.790 --> 22:47.560
<i>The words that I said that day
are still tightening my chest.</i>

22:47.630 --> 22:56.400
<i>A single shadow looked like light
in this world that I'm imprisoned in.</i>

22:56.470 --> 23:05.210
<i>The rain of May became lighter
as it was kindly shining tomorrow.</i>

23:05.280 --> 23:09.610
<i>I lost the meaning of smiling...</i>

23:09.680 --> 23:13.980
<i>... that day I thought I
lost my place to be.</i>

23:14.050 --> 23:18.420
<i>I wished for your warmth.</i>

23:18.490 --> 23:22.930
<i>We have stopped time.</i>

23:23.160 --> 23:27.260
<i>I had this feeling it was
eventually going to come, but...</i>

23:27.330 --> 23:31.900
<i>... I pretended I didn't know
and buried my loneliness.</i>

23:31.970 --> 23:42.080
<i>I looked down at your feet as the
droplets describing "Good-bye" fell.</i>

23:42.720 --> 23:51.450
<i>I hope that everything that
makes you sad will all disappear.</i>

23:51.530 --> 23:59.900
<i>The words that I said that day
are still tightening my chest.</i>

24:01.940 --> 24:05.030
Our secret that cannot
be known by anyone.

24:06.170 --> 24:10.740
The unorthodox power that
no one can understand.

24:12.480 --> 24:16.310
Bottomless evil intentions
eat into Naoya's heart.

24:17.790 --> 24:21.380
The hostility of frankness provokes me.

24:22.920 --> 24:29.860
<i>Next episode, "Touch."</i>

24:25.890 --> 24:28.730
Where are we headed?
